"hadiths[98]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2287,"From this chain of command, there is a similar tradition from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
2288,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sucking milk once or twice does not prove haraam."""
2289,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyida Umm al-Fazl (RA) that a companion came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I married a woman and I also had a second wife, so this first wife said that I have suckled this new bride once or twice, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sucking once or twice is not forbidden."""
2290,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: In the Holy Qur'an, this ruling was revealed that drinking milk ten times becomes haram (i.e., marriage becomes forbidden), then this ruling was abrogated by drinking milk five times, then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, died."
2291,"Hajjaj bin Hajjaj Aslami narrated from his father (Sayyidna Hajjaj, may God be pleased with him) that he said: O Messenger of God! What will take away my right to milk? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A slave or a concubine."""
2292,"Abdullah bin Abi Malikah said: Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Harith (may God be pleased with him) narrated the hadith to me, then he said: No, not from me, but I heard him narrating the hadith to the people that I married the daughter of Abu Ahab (bin Uzair) and a black woman came and said: I have breastfed you both (husband and wife). He turned away from me, (he repeated this request), Abu Asim said: The third or fourth time when Sayyiduna Uqbah (RA) inquired, he (SAW) said: How (will you have relations with this girl) and it has been said about her (i.e. you two are brothers and sisters sharing milk) and he (PBUH) stopped Sayyiduna Uqbah (RA) from going to that girl. Abu Asim said: Amr bin Saeed bin Abi Hussain only mentioned this word from Ibn Abi Malikah (""Faqeef waqd qil"") and did not say it (""Nahah"
2293,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him. At that time, a man was sitting near him. His face changed into a blessed one, and when he saw signs of displeasure on the blessed one's face, he said: This is my milk-sharing brother."
2294,"Sayyida Aisha (may God be pleased with her) said: Sayyida Sahlah bint Suhail bin Amr (may God be pleased with her) who was married to Sayyidna Abu Hudhayfah bin Utbah bin Rabiyyah (may God be pleased with him) attended the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Abu Hudhayfah’s slave Salim comes to our house and I am in the modest clothes of the house, and we consider him as our child, and Abu Hudhayfah adopted him like the Prophet. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) adopted Sayyiduna Zayd bin Harithah (RA) until this verse was revealed: However, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to breastfeed Salem. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Breastfeeding an older man was only for Salim. In other words, if someone drinks a lot of milk, it will not be considered sacred."
2295,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the one who made Halaah and the one for whom Halaah was made.
2296,"It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (RA) that Hind (bint Utbah) the mother of Muawiya and the wife of Sayyidna Abu Sufyan (RA) came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, he does not give me enough money that is enough for me and my children, but if I take something in their ignorance, then will it be a sin for me to do so? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""According to the habit, you can take enough wealth that is enough for you and your children."""
2297,"Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The best of you is the one who treats his family well, and when one of you dies, leave him alone."""
2298,"Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: When I got married to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I was six years old. Then we migrated to Madinah and stayed with Banu Harith bin Khazraj. When I came here, I got a fever and because of that my hair started falling out. I didn't know what they wanted to do with me. Finally, they took my hand and made me stand near the door of the house and I was breathing. After a while, when I calmed down, they took some water and splashed it on my face and head. Then they took me inside the house. There were some women of the Ansar who saw me and prayed that Allah would bless and bless you. My mother handed me over to them and they decorated me. Later in the day, suddenly the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and these women handed me over to him, and at that time I was nine years old."
2299,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, then Sayyiduna Umar mentioned it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, so he said: “Tell them to turn back and keep her (the wife) until the period of purification begins, then the periods come and then the purification begins, then if you wish, keep her with you and if you wish, divorce her. Before intercourse, then this is the Idda which Allah has ordered that women should be divorced."" (That is, this is the period that Allah has given in the command («fatalkohan laadtahn»)."
2300,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that when he divorced his wife, Sayyidna Umar (RA) mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him), and he (peace be upon him) said: “Tell them to take back this woman (i.e., resort to divorce) then, if they wish, divorce her in a state of purity.” Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Ibn al-Mubarak and al-Wakee narrated that in the state of pregnancy. (That is, either divorce the woman in a state of chastity, or divorce the woman when she is pregnant)."
2301,Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) divorced (his daughter) Sayyida Hafsa (RA) and then returned.
2302,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with him) and then returned to her. 
 Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Ibn al-Madini, may God have mercy on him, denied this hadith, and said that no one narrated it to us in Basra except Hameed."
2303,"Al-Haqam said: Yahya bin Hamza said to me that I say with certainty that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote for the people of Yemen that ""only a pure man should touch the Holy Qur'an, and divorce is not valid before marriage ownership, and freedom is not possible before purchase."" 
 Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked about Sulaiman, and he said: It was probably from the book of Umar bin Abdul Aziz."
2304,"Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha (RA) said that the wife of Rafa’ Al-Qurzi attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (SAW), at that time Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) was with him and Sayyidna Khalid bin Sa’eed bin Al-Aas (RA) was at the door asking to attend the service of the Messenger of Allah (SAW). The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Do you want to go to Rafa'ah? No, until he (the second husband) tastes your taste and you taste his taste"" (this is a reference to sexual intercourse). Upon hearing this, Sayyidna Khalid bin Saeed (RA) called out to Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA): Don't you see how this woman is talking loudly in front of the Prophet (PBUH)?"
2305,"Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: Sayyidna Rafa’ah (RA) who was a member of Banu Qurayzah, divorced his wife three times. After that, Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Zubair (RA) married her. Then that woman came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! They have (sharamgah) like this cloth (i.e. they are impotent and cannot have sexual intercourse), the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Perhaps you want to go to Rafa'ah again? No, it cannot be until she tastes your taste Abdur Rahman"" or he said, ""You do not taste her."""
2306,"Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about giving the authority to divorce, and she said: We were given the authority by the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, so did this mere authority become divorce?"
2307,"Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A woman who divorces her husband without reason is forbidden to smell the fragrance of Paradise."""
2308,"Umrah bint Abd al-Rahman reported that Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays bin Shamas (RA) had married Sayyida Habiba bint Sahl. Sayyida Habiba (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) intended to marry her and she was a neighbor of him (infard bi al-Darmi). Sayyidna Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) beat her, so she came to the door of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) in the morning. When the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) came out, he saw the shadow of a man. He said: I am Habiba bint Sahl. He said: ""What is the matter?"" They said: I am not or Thabit is not (that is, I cannot live with them), then when Sayyidna Thabit came to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: ""Take your wealth from him and leave him."" Whatever they gave is safe with me. So Sayyidna Thabit took all his possessions and left him, and Sayyida Habiba went and sat in her Makkah (i.e. divorced her husband)."
2309,"Saeed, a man from Banu Abdul Muttalib, said: I received the hadith of Abdullah bin Ali bin Yazid bin Raqana, and he was in his village, so I went to him and asked him, and he said: My father narrated the hadith to me. Said: ""What was your intention?"" He said: There was an intention to divorce. He said: ""By Allah, was the intention only one?"" He said: By Allah, the intention was the same. He said: ""What was your intention was the divorce."" That is, only one divorce took place."
2310,"Sayyidna Salama bin Sakhr Bayazi (RA) said: I used to have sexual intercourse with my wives so much that no one else would do it, so when the month of Ramadan came, I was afraid that I might do something with my wife that would not leave her bad until the morning, so I made Zahar for the end of Ramadan (i.e. told her to stay away that you are like my mother). When morning came, I went to my tribe and narrated this incident and said, ""Come with me to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."" He went to the Messenger of Allah and narrated his story to him, so he said: ""Have you done this?"" He said: I have done such a thing, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have you done such a thing?"" He said: Yes, I am guilty of it, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Salama! Did you commit this act?"" He said: Yes, I have committed such an act, and O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, I am present and also patient with the command of Allah, so judge me according to what Allah commands. No, he said: ""Then feed sixty poor people with a wasaq of dates."" I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, we have prepared some food for the last night (that is, how can we feed the poor people if we are so needy). He said: ""Go to the person who receives the charity of Bani Zureeq, he will give you something, feed the sixty poor people with it and give the rest to him."" You should eat and feed your family. Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhr (RA) said: I came to my tribe and told them that I felt narrowness and bad opinion with you, on the contrary, I saw openness and good opinion with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and he (PBUH) ordered me to give charity to you."
2311,"It is narrated from Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays that her husband divorced her three times and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) provided her with accommodation and no alimony. Muslima said: I mentioned this to Ibrahim, and he said: Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: We will abandon the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah of His Messenger because of the saying of a woman? No, therefore, they have prescribed alimony and alimony for divorced women."
2312,"Sayyida Fatima bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated the hadith that when her husband divorced her for the third time, the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) ordered her to observe the Eid in the house of her cousin (Abdullah) bin Umm Maktoum."
2313,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said: We will abandon the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah of His Prophet because of the saying of a woman? No, for the woman who gets divorced three times, there is also a skani and alimony."
2314,There is a similar tradition from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him).
2315,"It is narrated from Aswad that Ameerul Momineen Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: We will not obey any woman in the religion of Allah. For a woman with triple talaq, there is also skini and alimony. 
 Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: For such a divorced woman, I do not have any education or maintenance."
2316,"Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman reported that he and Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) gathered with Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) and it was mentioned about a (pregnant) woman whose husband has died and after a few days she gives birth. There was a debate between the two of them about this, so Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) said: I am with my nephew Abu Salama, then he sent the slave of the close Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) to Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyida Umm Salama (RA), and he asked her this question. came (i.e. blood flowed after childbirth) and a man from Banu Abdul Dar whose surname was Abul Sanabal gave a message of marriage to Sayyida Sabiyah (radiyallahu anha) and told her that (after pregnancy) she had become halal for marriage. What, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them that ""she can marry."""
2317,"It is narrated from a close friend that Sayyidah Umm Salamah (RA) said: The husband of Sayyidah Sabiyah Bint Al-Harith (RAH) died and a few days after his death, Sayyidah Sabiyah (RAH) gave birth to a child, then the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered her to marry him."
2318,"Abu al-Sanabul (Ibn Baalik, may God be pleased with him) said: Sayyida Sabia bint Al-Harith, may God be pleased with him, became pregnant more than twenty nights after the death of her husband, and when she was freed from childbirth, she adorned him, i.e., made wedding items."
2319,"It is narrated from Aswad that Sayyida Sabi'ah (may Allah be pleased with her) conceived (a child) a few days after her husband's death and she became beautiful. (In other words, confirming the end of the period and giving permission for marriage and decoration.)"
2320,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a loved one for more than three days except for her husband."""
2321,"Zainab bint Abi Salama narrates that Umm al-Momineen Sayyidah Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with her) had a brother or some other relative die (on the third day of Kuma fi al-Bukhari), she called for safra (perfume) and applied it to her hands (and cheeks) and said: I have done this because the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for any woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to marry her husband.” Mourning someone else for more than three days, mourning the husband for four months and ten days."
2322,"From this document, it is similar to the above-mentioned tradition."
2323,"On the authority of Sayyidah Umm Atiya, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman should not mourn for her husband for more than three days at any cost. is.”"
2324,"On the authority of Zainab bint Ka'b bin Ajra, Sayyidah Fareeah bint Malik (may Allah be pleased with her) informed her that she asked the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) to allow him to return to his Mecca, because my husband had gone out in search of his runaway slaves and caught them, but those slaves killed him near Qadum (the name of a place near Madinah). The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""You stay in your house until the period is completed."" So, I performed Idda for four months and ten days in that place, then when Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) became the caliph, he sent a messenger to me and inquired about it."
2325,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may God be pleased with him) said: My aunt got divorced and she wanted to pick some fruit from her garden, so a companion said to her that you cannot leave the house during ``iddah."
2326,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha (RA) that when they intended to buy Sayyida Barirah (RA), her owners wanted to make a bet on the inheritance of Sayyida Barirah (RA) (that is, we will sell her, but her walaah will be for us). Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: So I bought Barirah and freed her, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed her to live with her husband who was free, and meat was offered to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: “Where did it come from?” It was narrated: Sadaqah came for Barira. He said: ""It was a charity for him and a gift from him for us."""
2327,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and I offered food that did not contain meat. I said: O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace! That meat was given to Barira in charity, and Barira gave it to us, and you do not eat charity. He said: ""It is charity for them and it is a gift from Barira for us."""
2328,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha (RA) that when he freed Sayyida Barirah (RA), her husband was a slave, and the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to exhort her about her husband (not to leave him), and she used to say: Is it not permissible for me to divorce him? He said: ""Yes, there is authority"", then Sayyida Barira said: Then I separated from him."
2329,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrated that the husband of Sayyida Barira (RA) was a slave whose name was Mughith, as if I saw him circumambulating before Sayyida Barira (RA) and his beard was wet with tears. is.” The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said to Sayyida Barira, may Allah be pleased with her: ""Reconsider your decision because he is the father of your child."" Saida Barira said: O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace! Is this your order? He said: ""No, I am recommending"". Sayyidah Barira said: Then (I do not need to revise it and) I do not want Mughees."
2330,"It was narrated from Abu Maimunah Sulaiman, a slave of the people of Madinah, that I was sitting next to Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) when a woman came to him and said that my husband wants to take my child. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I was present in the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and a woman came to him and said that my husband wants to take his children or my son, who would serve me and bring water for me from the well of Abu Anba. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""You two cast lots."" Then the husband of that woman came and said: Who will argue with me about my children or my son? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (to the child): ""Son, this is your father and this is your mother. Hold the hand of whoever you want to be with."" 
 And Asim said: Go with whomever of them you like, so the boy took hold of his mother's hand and she took him away."
2331,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A maidservant has two divorces and her period is two periods."" Abu Asim said: I heard this from Mazahir bin Aslam."
2332,"On the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in favor of the prisoners of Autas: ""One should not associate with a pregnant woman until she is pregnant (i.e., associate with her in tahr after giving birth), nor should one associate with a non-pregnant woman until she has a period (so that it is known that she is not pregnant)."""
2333,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The pen has been lifted from three people (i.e. their good and bad deeds are not impeached): from a sleeper until he wakes up, from a child until he becomes an adult, and from a madman until he regains his senses."" 
 Hammad in another tradition says matwa instead of majin, the meaning of both is the same, i.e. crazy or insane, until he comes to his senses."
2334,"Ameerul Momineen Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan Radiyallahu Anhu said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: ""It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except for one of three things, one of which is disbelief after faith (i.e. he becomes a Muslim after he becomes a disbeliever), or he commits adultery after marriage (he will be stoned), or a person who kills someone unjustly will be killed in retribution."""
2335,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The blood of any man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, except for three people (even if they are Muslims) are exempted from this. A life for a life, a married adulterer, and one who abandons his religion and separates from the community of Muslims."""
2336,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: (Sayyidna) Safwan Ibn Umayyah (RA) was sleeping in the mosque when a man came to him and pulled his cloak from under his head. Safwan woke up, ran after him and caught the thief, and took him to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! I was sleeping in the mosque and this person came and pulled my sheet from under my head, I ran and grabbed him. Upon hearing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered to cut off his (thief's) hand, Sayyiduna Safwan (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) my cloak is not so valuable that the poor man's hand should be cut off because of it."
2337,"Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""For a quarter of a dinar or more, the hand (of a thief) will be cut off."""
2338,Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) cut his hand in a shield worth three dirhams.
2339,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the case of a Makhzoomi woman who had stolen became important to the Quraish and they said: Who should talk to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this? Then he said: Who will be able to do this except Sayyiduna Osama Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu? They are the messengers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Sayyiduna Osama (RA) spoke to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and he (PBUH) said: ""Have you come to intercede in the limits of Allah?"" Then the Prophet (PBUH) stood up and gave a sermon and said: ""O people! The people before you were ruined because when a big man among them stole, they would let him go, but if a weak one stole, they would set a limit on him. By Allah, if Fatima bint Muhammad (PBUH) had also stolen, I would have cut off his hand."""
2340,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Umayyah Makhzoomi (RA) that a thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) who confessed to the theft, but the stolen property was not recovered from him. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""I believe you did not steal?"" He said: No, I have stolen. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""I understand that you have not stolen?"" He said: I have stolen. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said after this confession: ""Take him and cut off his hand, then bring him to me."" So the Companions cut off his hand and took him to the service. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ask for forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him."" The man asked for forgiveness and repented to Allah. On this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Forgive him, O Allah! Forgive him."""
2341,"Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: ""There is no prohibition against stealing fruit and bunches."""
2342,The previous example is mentioned in this document as well. The translation of the hadith is mentioned above.
2343,The previous example is mentioned in this document as well. The translation of the hadith is mentioned above.
2344,The previous example is mentioned in this document as well. The translation of the hadith has been given above.
2345,"Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: ""The hand should not be cut off in stealing fruits and bunches."""
2346,"The translation of this hadith has also been given above. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: What Abu Usamah (his name is Hamad bin Usamah) said is correct."
2347,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no punishment for the one who snatches away, and the one who takes away, and the one who betrays."""
2348,"It was narrated on the authority of Anas that a person was brought to the Holy Prophet who had drunk alcohol, and he beat him with two sticks, then Abu Bakr did the same. is (in slander), so Sayyiduna Umar (RA) enforced it."
2349,"Huzain bin Munzar Qashi narrated that I was present with Sayyidna Uthan bin Affan (RA) when Waleed bin Uqbah (Akhiafi brother of Sayyidna Uthman RA) was brought. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a drunkard forty lashes, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may God be pleased with him) also gave him forty lashes, and Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) gave eighty lashes, and this is all Sunnah."
2350,"Amr bin Sharid narrated from his father: He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""When one of you drinks, beat him, then drink again and beat him, then if he drinks for the fourth time, kill him."""
2351,"Sayyiduna Abu Burda Hani bin Nayyar (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: ""No one should be punished with more than ten lashes except for one of the limits of Allah."""
2352,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that a Companion of the tribe of Islam came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and stated that he had committed adultery with him and he confessed four times that he had committed adultery, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered to stone him because he was married."
2353,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Samrah (may God be pleased with him) said: Ma'ez bin Malik (may God be pleased with him) was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (may God's prayers and peace be upon him) who was wearing a pistachio waistcoat and had no cloak on him. At that time, the Prophet (peace be upon him) was leaning on a pillow on his left. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Take them and stone them"", then he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Bring them back"", then the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, spoke to them. When they go out for Jihad, someone stays behind and bleats like a goat (i.e. the way a goat makes a sound when mating) and drops a little milk for them (milk means semen, i.e. commits adultery)."
2354,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira, Sayyidna Zayd bin Khalid and a young man said: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: I swear by Allah that you judge between us by the Book of Allah. Allow me to say something. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Say, what do you say?"" So it happened that my son was a servant in this man's house and he committed adultery with his wife. I gave him a hundred goats and a servant in exchange for it. I asked the people of knowledge and they told me that my son must be punished with one hundred lashes and one year of banishment from the city, and his wife must be circumcised. The Messenger of Allah, upon hearing this, said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my life, I will judge between you according to the Book of Allah. You will get back a hundred goats and servants, and your son will be given a hundred whips and he will be exiled for a year."" The woman confessed and Anees stoned her."
2355,"Abu Haitham bin Nasr bin Dahr Aslami narrated from his father Sayyiduna Nasr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was one of those who stoned him (Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him) that is, at the time of the stoning of Maaz bin Malik Aslami, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when the stones hit him, he was very afraid of the torture."
2356,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Take Ma'ez bin Malik and stone him"", so we took him to Baqi' al-Ghurqad and by Allah we did not tie him up or dig a hole, only he stood up and we killed him by throwing bones, sticks and stones at him."
2357,"Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father (Sayyidna Buraidah, may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man named Maaz bin Malik came, and he confessed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he had committed adultery. They were taken down and the people were ordered by the Prophet to stone them, so the people killed them in this way."
2358,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that the Jews brought to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) a man and a woman who had committed adultery. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""When one of you committed adultery, how did you treat them?"" They said: We do not find any command of this in the Torah. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam Radiyallahu Anhu said: You are a liar, there is Ayat al-Jum in the Torah, if you are truthful, bring the Torah and read it. (Raised his hand) So they saw that this is the verse of stoning, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered and they were stoned to death near the mosque where funerals were held. 
 Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I saw the woman's companion leaning on her trying to protect her from the stones."
2359,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: Sayyidna Umar, may God be pleased with him, said: Allah sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth and sent down upon him the Book (Quran), which contained the verse of stoning, which we read, memorized and understood, and then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, also stoned (the adulterer). After him, we also stoned (the adulterer). After passing away, someone starts saying that we do not find the verse of stoning in the Holy Quran. Although in the Book of Allah, stoning is a right and proof for a married man or woman who commits adultery, as long as evidence is found for adultery, or pregnancy is revealed or by confession."
2360,Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) said: I testify that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) reciting: Allah and Allah is Great and Wise».
2361,"Abdullah bin Burida narrated from his father, he said: I was sitting next to the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, when a woman from the Banu Ghamad tribe came to him and said: O Prophet of God! I have committed adultery and I want you to cleanse me (of this sin). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Go back"". Purify me, perhaps you are returning me as you returned Ma'az. By Allah, I am pregnant. Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Go back now and come when the birth is done."" The child was born, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Go and breastfeed him, come again when he stops milking""."
2362,"It was narrated on the authority of Imran bin Hussain that a woman from the Jahina tribe came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had become pregnant as a result of adultery. I have committed a deed, establish a deed on me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, called her guardian and said: ""Take her and keep her well, when she gives birth, bring her to me."" So he did so, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered about her and her clothes were tied tightly, then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered and she was stoned, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon her, prayed over her, Sayyiduna Umar. Radiyallahu Anhu said: O Messenger of Allah! You are praying over the one who committed adultery? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""He has repented in such a way that if his repentance was distributed among seventy men of the people of Medina, it would spread to all of them. Have you seen a better man than him who sacrificed his life for the sake of Allah?"""
2363,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Zaid bin Khalid Jahni and Sayyidna Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about an unmarried slave who committed adultery. He said, “If she commits adultery, flog her, then commit adultery, then flog her, then commit adultery, then flog her.” So sell it, even if it is only for a rope” (i.e. sell it for as little as a rope)."
2364,"On the authority of Sayyidina Ubada bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Get (the rules of the Sharia) from me, get (the rules of religion) from me. Allah has made a way for these women. A virgin boy commits adultery with a virgin girl, his punishment is one hundred lashes and one year's exile, and if a married man commits adultery with a married woman, his punishment is one hundred lashes and stoning."""
2365,"From this chain of transmission, Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrated the same narration from the Prophet (PBUH)."
2366,"It was narrated from Habib bin Salem that a boy named Qarqur had intercourse with his wife's slave girl. This matter was brought to Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (the ruler of Kufa), who said: I will make a positive decision about this. If so, I will stone this slave. This woman was asked: What do you say to your husband? This woman said: I had made my slave girl lawful for my husband (i.e. I had allowed sexual intercourse with her), so Sayyiduna Nu'man (RA) gave her a hundred lashes. 
 Yahya bin Hamad (Shaykh al-Darmi) said: It is rejected."
2367,This hadith has been narrated by Sadaqah bin Al-Fazl on the authority of Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer (RA) on the authority of the Prophet (PBUH).
2368,"Ibn Khuzima bin Thabit narrates from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever is punished for a crime, that sin is forgiven."" (That is, a person on whom the restriction is issued becomes free from this sin.)"
2369,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, a woman vowed to perform Hajj, but she died, so her brother came to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and inquired about it. He said: Yes, he would have paid it. He said: ""Fulfill this vow, it is more worthy of loyalty."""
2370,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) that I had taken a vow during the days of Jahiliyyah and then embraced Islam? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then fulfill your vow."""
2371,"Sayyidna Uqbah bin Amir Jahni (RA) said: His sister took a vow that she would go on foot and bareheaded for Hajj. I mentioned this to the Prophet (PBUH) and he (PBUH) said: ""Tell your sister to cover her head and ride and fast for three days."" (i.e. give expiation for not fulfilling the vow)."
2372,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) that the sister of Sayyidna Uqbah (RA) vowed that she would go to Baitullah Sharif on foot. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Indeed, Allah is rich with the vow of your sister. She should ride and sacrifice a sacrifice as an atonement."""
2373,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, found an old companion walking between his two sons and asked, ""What happened to this old man?"" (who walk with our support) His sons replied, O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace! He vowed to go (for Hajj) on foot. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O elder! Get on board, for Allah is rich with you and your vow."" (That is, Allah Ta'ala does not need it. It is in Bukhari Sharif: ""Allah Ta'ala is unconcerned (rich) about this person putting his life in punishment."")"
2374,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""One should not fulfill a vow of sin and disobedience, nor should he fulfill a vow that the son of Adam does not have the authority (i.e. power) to make."""
2375,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has vowed to obey Allah should obey Allah, and whoever has vowed to commit a sin should not commit a sin."""
2376,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that a person said: O Messenger of Allah! I had taken a vow that if Allah Ta'ala grants you the victory of Makkah, then I will go to Bayt al-Maqdis and pray. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Pray here (in the Kaaba)."" He repeated his question three times, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Now it is your will"" (meaning you have the right to go to Bait-ul-Maqdis and pray there and fulfill your vow)."
2377,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Nazr cannot return anything, only money comes out of the miser through it."""
2378,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) heard Sayyidna Umar Ibn Al-Khattab (RA) swearing by his father in a caravan, so he said: ""Indeed, Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers and forefathers, so whoever wants to swear an oath, let him swear by Allah, otherwise he should remain silent."""
2379,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever takes an oath and then says Insha'Allah, then he has made an exception."" (That is, even if he does not fulfill the oath now, expiation will not be obligatory on him.)"
2380,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever takes an oath to do something and at the same time says, ""Insha'Allah"", he has the right to fulfill the oath if he wants to, or not to fulfill it if he wants to."""
2381,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA): ""Do not swear."" Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is a long hadith. 
 It has been mentioned in Hadith No. (2193)."
2382,"Abdullah bin Amr, narrating the hadith during the Battle of Jamajum, said: A man asked Sayyiduna Udi bin Hatim for help, so he swore that he would not give him anything, then he said: I wish I had not heard from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was saying: ""If a man swears by something and then thinks it is good, he should first do what is best and then pay for his oath."""
2383,"Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: ""O Abd al-Rahman bin Samrah! Do not ask for government (emirship or governorship), because if you are given an emirship by asking, you will be handed over to it, and if you are given an emirship without asking, you will be helped in it (by Allah), and if you swear by something and then see good in something other than it, then atone for your oath."" Do what is good."""
2384,The above-mentioned hadith is also narrated from this chain of transmission.
